  "channel_name": "Sebastian Hardy | AI Marketing",
  "transcript": "CLI-Anything is a free open-source tool from HKUDS, the Hong Kong lab behind LightRAG, and it lets Claude Code drive desktop software that was never built for AI. Seventy ready-made connections ship with it, covering Blender, GIMP, Inkscape, Audacity, LibreOffice, OBS, Krita and Obsidian. It does not click your screen like a robot, it reads each program's own automation engine and drives it directly, which is why it holds up on real batch work. Install it with pip install cli-anything-hub, then ask for what you want in plain English. If you are learning Claude Code or looking for a real AI automation setup, start here.\n\nGet the full setup guide here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1C3jRTnhSjdlH2RGu5vaTArxuunabX5FLzwfYoR_HBrM/edit?usp=sharing\n\n#Shorts #ClaudeCode #AIAutomation",
